{
  "intent": "check_and_fix",
  "intent_description": "Investigate why monitoring pings to 172.16.0.12 are failing (25/25 lost). Impact: monitoring reports server unreachable. Desired outcome: determine root cause and restore/confirm ICMP reachability from the monitoring origin (server reachable from monitoring).",
  "target": "router2 GigabitEthernet0/0/0",
  "diagnosis": {
    "initial_alert_condition": "Monitoring reported 25 pings sent to 172.16.0.12 with 0 successful responses.",
    "observations": [
      "R2 GigabitEthernet0/0/0 admin_state=up oper_state=up, input_errors=0 output_errors=0 (interface is up and healthy).",
      "From router2, ping to 172.16.0.12 succeeded (5/5) with 1-2 ms RTT.",
      "Router configs: R2 has LAN 172.16.0.1/24 and OSPF advertises 172.16.0.0/24; routers show OSPF adjacencies between R1-R2-R3.",
      "No router-wide ACL observed that explicitly denies ICMP to 172.16.0.12 in the collected configs. (R1 and R2 have extended ACLs but they target TCP ports and different source/destination networks.)"
    ],
    "root_causes": [],
    "missing_info": [
